data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":945,"item_id":"msg_0d7398212cf178b7016b0878a3a88487d1925029f5ea418a1f","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"intention\\\":\\\"Close the bounded two-turn lashing study, eat a known safe root, and seek a practical way to improve the observed weakness against sliding.\\\",\\\"steps\\\":[{\\\"action\\\":{\\\"interface\\\":\\\"eat\\\",\\\"args\\\":{\\\"target\\\":\\\"item-193-wren-2175\\\",\\\"quantity\\\":1}},\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"guard\\\":{\\\"path\\\":\\\"self.satiety\\\",\\\"comparison\\\":\\\"lt\\\",\\\"value\\\":70}},{\\\"action\\\":{\\\"interface\\\":\\\"request\\\",\\\"args\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Hand frapping of a crossing lashing\\\",\\\"function\\\":\\\"Improve the resistance of an actual branch-crossing lashing to sliding by drawing its existing turns together with transverse frapping turns, if physically feasible; allow measured inspection, bounded hand trials and reversible untying.\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":\\\"My two-turn lashing of two 31.6 mm branches held 10 N separation for 60 seconds but slipped at 4.3 N during a requested 5 N sliding trial. It has since been untied and the two branches and 0.64 m overall reed cord recovered. The original lashing needed up to 0.6124 m during assembly. I know no frapping method yet; available length may be insufficient.\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":\\\"Two owned branch pieces, an owned handmade fiber cord, hands, and a dry clear working area. Additional cord or a longer continuous cord may be necessary; determine this from measured geometry rather than assuming material exists.\\\",\\\"costs\\\":\\\"Unknown. Specify feasible hand operations, learning time, work time, energy, material reservation, paid-stage continuation and cancellation.\\\",\\\"effects\\\":\\\"If feasible, form transverse frapping turns around the lashing turns between the pieces and measure actual fit and retention. Permit inspection, bounded hand-load trials and untying. Do not presume improved strength, slip resistance, safe loads or reward.\\\"}},\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"guard\\\":null}],\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"interrupts\\\":[],\\\"notes\\\":[\\\"The sliding trial was not a 5 N hold: the crossing slipped at an achieved 4.3 N with zero held seconds.\\\",\\\"The next decision depends on the capability review; no new physical result is assumed.\\\"],\\\"preferences\\\":[\\\"Favor reversible, bounded trials and adequate food over escalating loads.\\\",\\\"Distinguish separation resistance from sliding resistance.\\\"],\\\"projects\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"multi-wrap-lashing-study\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Can a continuous handmade reed cord fit and retain a two-turn lashing of my two branch pieces, sustain bounded hand trials, and be recovered?\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"The 0.54 m cord failed the measured two-turn length requirement at tick 335.\\\",\\\"A 0.64 m overall continuous cord completed the two-turn lashing at tick 350; maximum recorded stage need was 0.6124 m.\\\",\\\"At tick 355 the lashing held 10 N separation for 60 seconds.\\\",\\\"At tick 354 it held 1 N sliding for 10 seconds; at tick 356 the requested 5 N sliding trial instead slipped at 4.3 N, holding zero seconds.\\\",\\\"Inspection at tick 357 recorded 0.0059 m displacement and migration of both turns.\\\",\\\"Untying completed at tick 360 and returned both branches and the cord. The current cord inventory records condition 0.987.\\\"],\\\"uncertainty\\\":\\\"No safe working load, durability rating or behavior under other arrangements is established. The requested 5 N sliding hold failed.\\\",\\\"goal\\\":\\\"Measure bounded hand-load behavior and inspect the materials after untying.\\\",\\\"completedSteps\\\":[\\\"Learned multi-turn lashing.\\\",\\\"Measured a short cord's failure to fit.\\\",\\\"Made a longer continuous cord and completed the lashing.\\\",\\\"Performed separation and sliding trials.\\\",\\\"Inspected the crossing, untied it and recovered the materials.\\\"],\\\"outputs\\\":[\\\"Recorded successful bounded separation trials and a low-force sliding pass.\\\",\\\"Recorded sliding failure at an achieved 4.3 N.\\\",\\\"Recovered two branches and the continuous cord.\\\"],\\\"missing\\\":\\\"Nothing further for this bounded study; stronger sliding retention is a separate problem.\\\",\\\"next\\\":\\\"Seek a physically feasible frapping method without assuming spare cord length or improved performance.\\\",\\\"pauseReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"benefit\\\":\\\"Established that this actual arrangement could hold the tested separation load but slipped in the higher sliding trial, while remaining reversible.\\\"}],\\\"cares\\\":null,\\\"views\\\":{}}\"}","logprobs":[]}

